# Overview

This version of the Solace Message Utility takes on a completely different architecture to allow for modularization of the utility.

It now supports both queue browsing and discovery with.

Please read the below user guide to understand more on the finer details of each feature.

# 🔌 Connections


This page handles the different connection sessions required for the rest of the modules to work:

| Connection Type | Modules supported |
| - | - |
| SEMP | - Queue Discovery |
| Client | - Queue Browsing |

![Connections](images/connections.png)

> In order to reduce discrepancies and user input error, both connections must share the same hostname / IP.

## Solace Client Connection

Supports both Basic and OAuth2 authentication mechanism.

Please ensure you have entered the correct details:
- Protocol
- Port
- Message VPN

For Basic Auth:
- Username
- Password

For OAuth2 Auth:
- Access Token
- ID Token

## SEMP Connection

Please ensure you have entered the correct details:
- Protocol
- Port
- Username
- Password

> Other SEMP connection (e.g. via client or OAuth2) will be available in the future.

# 🔍 Queue Discovery

After establishing a SEMP connection, a list of Message VPNs on the broker will be available for browsing. You can then select the queue to browse instead of having to enter the queue name manually.

![Queue Discovery](images/discovery.png)

# 📂 Queue Browser

After establishing a Solace Client connection, you would be able to bind to a queue to browse messages on the queue.

![Queue Discovery](images/browser.png)

The browser has the following features:
- Bind to multiple queues
- View messages and their content
- Filter / Search message(s)
- Download message(s)
- Forward (Resend) message(s) to a different destination
- Delete message(s)

## Binding to Queue(s)

Enter the queue name to bind. You can bind multiple queues and bound queues will be available in the `Bound Queues` dropdown list.

## View Message and Message Content

After a queue is bound, the message list will be populated with messages on the queue.

The browser will show the full message content (header properties + payload):

**Key properties are displayed in its own field:**

| Field | Description |
| - | - |
| `Message Id` | This is the Guaranteed Message Identifier (`msg.getGuaranteedMessageId()`) or also known as the `Spooler Message Identifier`. This is more of an internal identifier that the Solace Event Broker uses and should not be used by an application for processing. |
| `Destination` | This is the immediate destination (queue name or the topic string) that the message is sent to. <br> If a message is sent to a topic and reaches the queue via the queue’s topic subscription, the destination field will capture the original topic string | 
| `Replication Group Message Id` | This is the unique identifier that applications should use to uniquely identify the message. This identifier will be the same for all copies of the message that is received. |

**Additional message header / properties are displayed in `Message Properties` section as key-value pairs:**
- Application Message Id
- Cache Request Id
- Correlation Id
- Delivery Count
- Delivery Mode
- HTTP Content Encoding
- HTTP Content Type
- Priority
- Reply To
- Sender Id
- Sequence Number
- Time to Live
- Topic Sequence Number

Application / User-defined / Custom Message Properties are displayed in `Application / User Properties` section as key-value pairs.

The payload / body is displayed in `Content Preview` section.

## Filter / Search Message(s)

![Queue Discovery](images/browser-filter.png)

You can filter / search messages using any part of the messages:

| Field | Description | Case Insensitive | Exact Match | Supports Wildcard |
| - | - |
| `Message Id` | Matches Guaranteed Message Identifier | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |
| `Message Type` | Matches Message Types (e.g. Text, Binary, Map, Stream, or Any | | ✔ | ✔ |
| `Destination Name` | Matches Queue Name or Topic String | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |
| `Destination Type` | Matches Queue or Topic | | ✔ | ✔ |
| `Properties Filter` | Matches both Message Properties and Application / User Properties | ✔ | ✔ | ✔ |
| `Body Content` | Matches body payload. Wildcard is automatically applied | ✔ | | |

> Use `*` for fields that support wildcard to perform wildcard matches. `*` is treated as any characters (spaces and symbols included) 0 or more. <br>
> For fields that do not support exact match, they are always in wildcard mode e.g. entering `match text` will be equivalent to `*match text*`

Search criteria can be selected between ANY or ALL. ANY is equivalent to `OR` logic operator whereas ALL is equivalent to `AND` logic operator.
- ANY: Messages display matches **any** of the criteria
- ALL: Messages display matches **all** of the criteria

## Download Message(s)

There are 2 flavours of download option available:
1. Download message body only
2. Download full message object in JSON

Message download can be perform per message or in bulk.

> For Bulk Download to be available, the JSZip library must be made available. Place `jszip.

